# Full Product Preservation

Read `docs/FULL_PRODUCT_PRESERVATION_DIRECTIVE.md` before planning or editing Gummy OS.

## Locked law

```text
Simplify the doorway. Do not flatten the house.
```

The user-first shell is additive. It does not redefine Gummy OS as a generic assistant, storage client, or project manager.

Protected product pillars:

- Gummy OS shell and protocol;
- local approximately 4B Gummy Operator lane;
- VideoBoss (`bohselecta/videoboss`);
- ImageHoss (`bohselecta/imagehoss`);
- 3D Bee (`bohselecta/3d-bee`);
- Actors, Actor Homes, Bowls, Links, Grabs, rooms, and the Social Layer;
- Local and managed Gummy Box plus optional GitHub/Drive connectors;
- production branding and current migrations.

Do not remove, rename away, hide indefinitely, or replace these pillars because they are outside one implementation lane.

Do not copy specialist repositories wholesale. Integrate through a first-party app registry, versioned contracts, truthful launch modes, and protocol adapters.

Before any broad shell, storage, or conversation rewrite, return a gap audit covering all protected pillars and state exactly what will and will not change.

Do not merge or flatten the product without explicit founder authorization.
